(with \eqn{r_i = 1}{r_i = 1} if \eqn{i}{i} responds), applied as
\eqn{w_i \leftarrow f_c w_i}{w_i <- f_c * w_i}. A response-propensity model
instead adjusts unit by unit, \eqn{w_i \leftarrow w_i / \hat\phi_i}{w_i <- w_i / phi_hat_i},
